        {
          "kicker": "Club rugby",
          "heading": "Club: George Hendy stars as Northampton end England's Champions Cup duck",
          "body": "In club rugby, Northampton beat Cardiff 28-12 to deliver the first Premiership win of the Champions Cup's opening round, after seven English rivals had failed to claim one. Uncapped winger George Hendy set up the opening try with an aerial catch and run from halfway and touched down again in the second half. Director of rugby Phil Dowson said, \"George can break the game open,\" while England's scrum-half Alex Mitchell also caught Planet Rugby's eye ahead of the November squad announcement."
        },
