      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Champions Cup",
          "heading": "Montpellier club grind Bath down 32-14 in Champions Cup opener",
          "body": "Top 14 club Montpellier came from four points down at the break to beat Bath 32-14 at a sold-out Recreation Ground on the Champions Cup's opening weekend. Bath were outscored 22-0 after half-time, Adam Hastings having kept the visitors within range with a first-half penalty. Montpellier took the win on grit and guile, and were beaten finalists in the Top 14 last season."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Fiji's Jake White takes charge before Japan Test",
