      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Foley tribute",
          "heading": "Munster club: Tadhg Beirne hails Foley tribute win as \"exactly the performance\"",
          "body": "Munster's Champions Cup win over Racing 92 in Cork was a club occasion with a deep emotional thread: skipper Tadhg Beirne said the 33-25 victory was \"exactly the performance\" Anthony Foley would have been proud of, a decade after Foley died on the eve of the Racing match in Paris. Olive Foley presented the jerseys on Friday. Twenty-year-old Charlie O'Shea made his first Champions Cup start at No. 10 and contributed six points."
        },
