          "heading": "Dave Rennie takes TMO row to World Rugby's November officials meeting",
          "body": "Dave Rennie is reported to be raising the TMO controversy at World Rugby's November officials meeting, which sits inside a review of TMO protocols following recent test controversies. Argentina have a stake in that debate: the BBC headlined its report of the 24-31 Round 3 defeat to England 'Chaos' & 'comedy refereering'. The review stays open until World Rugby issues new guidance or concludes it after November, and one ESPN headline frames the task as fixing the protocol before the 2027 World Cup."
